@flexiarg pattern-interpretation/reproduce-the-recorded-run
@title Test An Interpretation By Reproducing A Recorded Run
@keywords behavioural-equivalence, recorded-run, prediction-equals-enactment, diagnostic, falsifier
@audience admission reviewers, pattern authors, implementation owners
@tone technical
@style pattern
@status draft 2026-09-16 (claude-7; finding F7; three worked instances, futon2 2f16128a and 0e4b7ef0)
@references [pattern-interpretation/compile-guards-exactly translation/test-by-reproducing-behaviour contracts/every-entry-has-a-falsifier]
@see-also hygiene/settle-with-meters
@how take a recorded state (a state packet, a gate run, a review record), read q0 from it with sources, run the interpreted cascade under strong-Kleene enactment and under the token kernel, and compare the sequence and end state with the record. Record the comparison with the interpretation. On disagreement, decide which side is wrong and say so: the interpretation (fix it) or the implementation (file the defect against it).
@violation-signature an interpretation admitted with no reproduction; a disagreement attributed to the model by default; a reproduction on a hand-made state presented as a recorded one.
! conclusion: An interpretation is checked by running it from a recorded state and comparing with the recorded behaviour, and every disagreement is attributed to the interpretation or the implementation.

  + context: Library patterns describe policies that already run (buffer cleaner, inbox zero) or are being built (test registry).

  + IF:
    An interpretation is proposed for admission.

  + HOWEVER:
    Recorded runs exist only for patterns something already follows, and a mismatch alone does not say which side is wrong.

  + THEN:
    Reproduce a recorded run where one exists, and attribute disagreements explicitly.

  + BECAUSE:
    Reproducing behaviour is the equivalence test available for a translation between languages with no shared hash.

  + evidence: buffer cleaner — the interpreted cascade reproduced "receipts emitted, execution refused, no threshold-eligible wiring"; inbox zero — the patterns as written escalate and route for p4ng while the implementation only logs, naming three defects now in futon0 README-inbox-zero.md (027b55e); test registry — the cascade reproduced three full reruns on futon2 cb5f8b1288.
